cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Nikasha or NikashaBench in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Nikasha: fact-checking vulnerability reports against source code at the claimed version"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rakshit
    family-names: Rameshbabu
    email: rakshitoffl@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0.dev0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rakshit-737/nikasha"
url: "https://github.com/rakshit-737/nikasha"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - security
  - vulnerability disclosure
  - vulnerability triage
  - bug bounty
  - CVE
  - static analysis
  - tree-sitter
  - AddressSanitizer
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Nikasha checks the factual claims in a vulnerability report (cited files, functions,
  line numbers, stack traces, quoted code, patches and options) against a project's source
  code at the exact version the report names, and can reproduce the claimed crash in a
  hardened container. It combines the evidence deterministically into an explainable
  verdict and drafts neutral follow-up questions for the reporter.
